WEBVTT

00:00.010 --> 00:03.770
[Breaking News] [High Fever Cases
Skyrocketing Globally]

00:00.930 --> 00:03.229
If what Skinner said is true,

00:03.230 --> 00:05.589
there are only six days left

00:05.590 --> 00:06.939
before the first death from Hapna.

00:06.940 --> 00:09.929
Right now, there is a sharp increase

00:09.930 --> 00:12.279
in suspected Hapna-induced fever cases.

00:12.280 --> 00:15.019
Hospitals are overflowing
with fever patients,

00:15.020 --> 00:17.680
and the medical system is
under extreme strain.

00:18.180 --> 00:21.509
Please don't go to the hospital
if you have a fever.

00:21.510 --> 00:24.180
Please take care of yourself at home.

00:24.120 --> 00:31.950
[Dow Jones Industrial Average]

00:24.260 --> 00:27.440
Stock prices are plummeting
uncontrollably.

00:27.610 --> 00:28.509
New York, Shanghai,

00:28.510 --> 00:32.020
and other major stock exchanges
have all closed.

00:31.990 --> 00:38.000
[Widespread Shutdowns Continue: Congress,
Financial Institutions, and Postal Services]

00:32.049 --> 00:34.549
Congress, banks, and post offices—

00:34.550 --> 00:36.229
all operations have ceased,

00:36.230 --> 00:38.260
with no signs of resuming.

00:38.050 --> 00:45.000
[Uncertain Future: Dr. Skinner's
Prediction Stirs Global Alarm and Action]

00:38.280 --> 00:39.839
For us,

00:39.840 --> 00:41.209
perhaps today

00:41.210 --> 00:43.890
is our last Sunday.

02:08.530 --> 02:14.670
[LAZARUS]

02:16.850 --> 02:17.659
This is

02:17.660 --> 02:19.349
an analysis report on the pill

02:19.350 --> 02:21.328
that Chris found in Skinner's room.

02:21.329 --> 02:22.649
Could it be

02:22.650 --> 02:24.789
some kind of antidote for Hapna
or something?

02:24.790 --> 02:25.629
No way.

02:25.630 --> 02:28.140
This is an antiplatelet drug,

02:28.329 --> 02:30.819
used to prevent blood clots.

02:30.820 --> 02:32.169
That's disappointing.

02:32.170 --> 02:35.559
It seems to be mainly used for patients
who have had artificial hearts implanted.

02:35.560 --> 02:36.730
Does that mean

02:36.930 --> 02:39.189
Skinner has an artificial heart?

02:39.190 --> 02:41.960
He's had heart disease for a long time,

02:42.180 --> 02:45.189
but I haven't heard that he
got an artificial heart.

02:45.190 --> 02:48.359
So he had an artificial heart implanted
within the past three years?

02:48.360 --> 02:49.939
But such a major surgery

02:49.940 --> 02:52.660
would've been hard to hide.

02:52.890 --> 02:54.549
Here's a list of hospitals
that have performed

02:54.550 --> 02:58.280
artificial heart implantation surgeries
in the past three years.

02:59.750 --> 03:01.500
No matches for him.

03:02.340 --> 03:05.910
What are you up to this time, bastard?

03:06.030 --> 03:08.650
The secret work of some genius surgeon?

03:08.790 --> 03:11.259
People like that don't exist in real life.

03:11.260 --> 03:12.730
Could it be

03:12.880 --> 03:15.299
some hospital

03:15.300 --> 03:16.949
that's only open to
a certain privileged class?

03:16.950 --> 03:18.470
What is that?

03:18.650 --> 03:19.909
Haven't you heard of it?

03:19.910 --> 03:22.069
Hospitals that, in exchange for
exorbitant fees,

03:22.070 --> 03:26.159
guarantee total privacy
for their patients.

03:26.160 --> 03:28.119
Then let's try starting from this angle.

03:28.120 --> 03:29.520
These kinds of hospitals

03:29.710 --> 03:31.859
operate on a referral-only basis.

03:31.860 --> 03:35.078
Ordinary people don't seem to know
such hospitals exist.

03:35.079 --> 03:36.219
Indeed.

03:36.220 --> 03:38.828
I can't find any trace of them
in the medical network.

03:38.829 --> 03:40.419
Does such a thing really exist?

03:40.420 --> 03:42.020
Could it be an urban legend?

04:01.590 --> 04:03.300
Axel, Doug,

04:04.050 --> 04:05.910
would you come with me somewhere?

04:07.560 --> 04:09.820
You, and with that outfit...

04:09.970 --> 04:12.750
Actually, I have some clues.

04:20.899 --> 04:25.070
[Episode 10: I Can't Tell You Why]

04:22.220 --> 04:23.120
Axel.

04:23.580 --> 04:25.190
Axel Gilberto.

04:26.200 --> 04:27.410
Where is he right now?

04:45.570 --> 04:46.760
I'm Leland.

05:08.690 --> 05:11.889
Is this a palace or something?

05:11.890 --> 05:14.299
Feels like where Batman would live.

05:14.300 --> 05:16.120
Drive us up to the main entrance.

05:27.290 --> 05:28.680
Young Master.

05:29.450 --> 05:30.650
Good to see you.

05:30.760 --> 05:32.550
At long last, you're back.

05:32.740 --> 05:33.710
Is this place

05:33.870 --> 05:35.440
your actual home?

05:35.620 --> 05:37.620
Um, thank you very much.

05:37.750 --> 05:39.129
The exit is that way.

05:39.130 --> 05:40.109
Grandpa.

05:40.110 --> 05:42.840
They are not chauffeurs.

05:42.970 --> 05:45.139
They're friends who've
really looked after me.

05:45.140 --> 05:46.000
I see.

05:47.340 --> 05:49.070
Excuse me.

05:49.390 --> 05:52.020
Welcome to the Astor family estate.

06:00.600 --> 06:03.039
What is the Astor family?

06:03.040 --> 06:04.280
You don't know?

06:04.910 --> 06:07.970
They're an old noble family
going back generations.

06:17.800 --> 06:21.249
Hey, aren't we, like,
a bit out of place here?

06:21.250 --> 06:22.729
How would I know?

06:22.730 --> 06:23.940
Oh my.

06:24.170 --> 06:26.260
What a surprise.

06:28.470 --> 06:30.160
Who could this be?

06:31.250 --> 06:34.430
It's been so long that I can't
even remember your name.

06:35.280 --> 06:38.250
So the prodigal son returns, huh?

06:38.620 --> 06:40.750
It's been a long time since we last met.

06:40.880 --> 06:42.900
I hope you've been well, sister.

06:43.250 --> 06:44.799
How could I be well,

06:44.800 --> 06:46.159
you brat?

06:46.790 --> 06:48.070
Today,

06:48.310 --> 06:49.909
I'm here to ask a favor of you.

06:50.100 --> 06:51.089
A favor?

06:51.090 --> 06:54.158
You haven't been home for four years,
and now you come back asking for a favor?

06:54.159 --> 06:55.409
What is it this time?

06:55.659 --> 06:57.340
Fraud? Theft?

06:57.540 --> 06:59.800
What do you need me to
smooth over for you?

07:01.200 --> 07:04.359
Father went to great lengths to
get you into that school,

07:04.360 --> 07:06.850
but you just kept screwing up.

07:07.740 --> 07:09.370
Back then,

07:09.660 --> 07:11.699
I really caused trouble for all of you.

07:11.700 --> 07:13.480
You were really troublesome.

07:14.180 --> 07:15.300
Please,

07:16.020 --> 07:18.089
could you tell me about
the membership-based medical society

07:18.090 --> 07:20.820
that the Astor family has always used?

07:21.120 --> 07:22.780
Recommend our doctors to you?

07:24.260 --> 07:26.690
What are you scheming this time?

07:29.760 --> 07:31.549
Seriously.

07:31.550 --> 07:34.810
Why is the only man left in this family
someone like you?

07:35.159 --> 07:38.409
If only Father had abolished
that outdated, wrong,

07:38.580 --> 07:42.158
male-only inheritance rule before he died.

07:42.159 --> 07:44.879
Is it really appropriate for us
to be here?

07:44.880 --> 07:46.419
Don't ask me.

07:46.420 --> 07:47.719
That being said,

07:47.720 --> 07:48.640
if...

07:49.020 --> 07:51.249
if you can find a matrilocal husband...

07:51.250 --> 07:53.049
Huh? What are you saying?

07:53.050 --> 07:53.989
Well...

07:53.990 --> 07:54.839
Miss Isabella...

07:54.840 --> 07:57.019
I've been set up on

07:57.020 --> 07:58.239
many arranged dates!

07:58.240 --> 08:00.620
To meet men I don't even like!

08:01.090 --> 08:02.749
Every single one of them

08:02.750 --> 08:06.180
is just after the fortune!

08:07.550 --> 08:10.230
You...

08:10.770 --> 08:13.430
don't even know anything!

08:23.510 --> 08:24.919
Please

08:24.920 --> 08:26.519
inherit everything from
the Astor family immediately.

08:26.520 --> 08:27.270
Eh?

08:28.190 --> 08:29.450
This way,

08:29.700 --> 08:32.250
you won't have to keep coming
to me for favors.

08:32.360 --> 08:34.058
All the information you want to know

08:34.059 --> 08:35.809
will be yours.

08:38.350 --> 08:41.030
You've always seen me as a nuisance.

08:42.159 --> 08:44.190
Just because our brothers all died,

08:44.370 --> 08:46.830
you suddenly want me
to inherit everything.

08:47.550 --> 08:48.949
I hardly have

08:48.950 --> 08:51.400
any memories of my father from childhood.

08:52.530 --> 08:54.119
Are you trying to say

08:54.120 --> 08:56.569
it's because you're an illegitimate child?

08:56.570 --> 08:58.250
So what?

08:58.660 --> 09:00.629
You yourself were being difficult
during your rebellious phase,

09:00.630 --> 09:02.690
doing all sorts of pointless things.

09:03.690 --> 09:05.660
When my mother passed away,

09:05.970 --> 09:07.770
Father didn't even show up.

09:08.050 --> 09:09.499
Well, that couldn't be helped.

09:09.500 --> 09:12.139
How could he possibly go to
his mistress's funeral?

09:12.140 --> 09:14.250
I didn't come to his funeral

09:15.290 --> 09:17.520
to get back at him for that.

09:19.130 --> 09:20.540
Enough.

09:20.920 --> 09:22.709
If you don't want to inherit this family,

09:22.710 --> 09:24.170
then don't ever come back.

09:32.250 --> 09:33.339
Why

09:33.340 --> 09:34.770
are we even here?

09:35.050 --> 09:36.859
Maybe to show us

09:36.860 --> 09:39.309
his so-called

09:39.310 --> 09:40.580
true self?

09:42.300 --> 09:44.359
Despite everything she said,

09:44.360 --> 09:46.459
but Miss Isabella has been looking forward

09:46.460 --> 09:47.579
to your return more than anyone,

09:47.580 --> 09:49.480
Young Master Leland.

09:50.210 --> 09:53.519
Just now, when she heard you were back,

09:53.520 --> 09:56.580
her face lit up as it hadn't in years.

10:07.510 --> 10:10.060
Why did things turn out like this?

10:10.990 --> 10:13.099
I originally swore

10:13.100 --> 10:14.920
I wouldn't argue with you today.

10:15.780 --> 10:17.529
On the anniversary of Father's death,

10:17.530 --> 10:20.729
there was a bouquet of white carnations
in front of his tombstone.

10:20.730 --> 10:21.699
That

10:21.700 --> 10:23.200
was from you, right?

10:23.490 --> 10:25.420
That...

10:25.780 --> 10:27.600
You left it there, right?

10:27.920 --> 10:28.820
Yes.

10:29.550 --> 10:30.669
Fine.

10:30.670 --> 10:31.939
I'll tell you.

10:31.940 --> 10:33.409
In return,

10:33.410 --> 10:35.769
you'll spend this weekend with me.

10:35.770 --> 10:36.700
Eh?

10:37.220 --> 10:39.330
The world's already like this.

10:39.800 --> 10:42.779
It's ending in a few days, right?

10:42.780 --> 10:44.319
Even if it's just a weekend,

10:44.320 --> 10:45.890
let's spend it together.

10:47.070 --> 10:48.249
That's the condition

10:48.250 --> 10:51.210
for telling you about our doctors.

10:52.150 --> 10:53.430
I understand.

10:54.570 --> 10:55.620
Next...

10:56.140 --> 10:58.890
next Sunday, I will definitely come back.

10:59.060 --> 11:00.900
Next Sunday?

11:01.420 --> 11:02.789
Haven't you seen the news?

11:02.790 --> 11:04.329
I'm asking you for this information

11:04.330 --> 11:08.350
so that we all get
another peaceful Sunday.

11:09.520 --> 11:11.140
Please.

11:12.530 --> 11:21.410
[LAZARUS]

11:31.980 --> 11:33.389
Thank you for your continued patronage,

11:33.390 --> 11:35.360
sir.

11:41.540 --> 11:42.810
May luck be with you.

11:43.290 --> 11:44.240
No,

11:44.580 --> 11:46.980
there's no such thing
as luck in this world.

11:48.290 --> 11:49.950
Do you have an appointment?

11:48.650 --> 11:53.370
[Exclusive Medical Society]

11:49.970 --> 11:52.470
I'm not here to see a doctor.

11:53.590 --> 11:55.560
Could you please inform her

11:55.790 --> 11:57.410
that Leland Astor is here?

11:58.230 --> 11:59.979
Oh, my.

11:59.980 --> 12:02.720
What a rare client.

12:02.840 --> 12:04.779
It hasn't been that long,

12:04.780 --> 12:06.950
but you've grown so much,

12:07.060 --> 12:08.159
Leland.

12:08.160 --> 12:09.780
It's been a long time.

12:10.050 --> 12:12.810
Cancel all my appointments for today.

12:13.000 --> 12:17.530
After all, they're all clients coming to
treat Hapna-related reactions anyway.

12:18.360 --> 12:20.950
I'd like you to confirm this.

12:21.340 --> 12:22.610
This video...

12:22.820 --> 12:24.180
Could it be...

12:24.920 --> 12:27.179
Yes, part of the surveillance video

12:27.180 --> 12:29.260
from the Schiphol Airport incident.

12:29.480 --> 12:30.879
Wasn't this already confiscated

12:30.880 --> 12:33.149
by the U.S. military in Europe?

12:33.150 --> 12:36.219
I managed to get part of the backup data.

12:36.220 --> 12:37.289
Where did you get it?

12:37.290 --> 12:39.000
It was leaked by an insider.

12:39.380 --> 12:41.749
When the world is just days away
from its end,

12:41.750 --> 12:43.660
you get a lot of people like that.

12:45.330 --> 12:46.519
Skinner...

12:46.520 --> 12:49.800
This is the video from twelve minutes
before the incident.

12:52.930 --> 12:54.379
That's right.

12:54.380 --> 12:56.019
It's him.

12:56.020 --> 12:59.009
We believe what Skinner was preparing to
take out there

12:59.010 --> 13:02.339
was Hapna's prototype reagent.

13:02.340 --> 13:04.019
Skinner...

13:04.020 --> 13:06.399
he must have wanted to reveal something.

13:06.400 --> 13:08.740
What happened after that is the problem.

13:09.780 --> 13:12.110
I quit long ago.

13:12.720 --> 13:14.939
But since the world is about to end,

13:14.940 --> 13:17.709
there's no point in holding off
on a cigarette now.

13:17.710 --> 13:19.000
Well...

13:19.210 --> 13:21.689
we're currently looking for Skinner.

13:21.690 --> 13:24.920
Did he ever undergo heart surgery here?

13:26.760 --> 13:29.519
I know this isn't something
you can tell us lightly,

13:29.520 --> 13:30.449
but

13:30.450 --> 13:33.660
this is our only clue related to Skinner.

13:34.030 --> 13:35.230
Please tell us.

13:41.060 --> 13:43.300
On the day of your father's funeral,

13:43.560 --> 13:45.550
you secretly came, didn't you?

13:45.870 --> 13:49.130
In order not to be found, you hid
in the corner of the church.

13:50.140 --> 13:51.900
I knew it then.

13:52.410 --> 13:55.069
You let the police get involved

13:55.070 --> 13:57.749
and were therefore isolated
by the Astor family.

13:57.750 --> 13:58.519
Even so,

13:58.520 --> 14:01.010
I always knew you were
a kind-hearted child.

14:01.790 --> 14:03.639
Now, doctor-patient confidentiality

14:03.640 --> 14:05.039
has become meaningless.

14:05.040 --> 14:06.219
Rather, perhaps

14:06.220 --> 14:07.269
I've been waiting all along,

14:07.270 --> 14:09.730
hoping for someone to come find me
like this.

14:10.090 --> 14:11.500
You just can't

14:11.730 --> 14:14.260
take something like this
to the grave, right?

14:14.710 --> 14:16.789
The unit that stormed in

14:16.790 --> 14:20.610
was the Delta Force, instructed by
the Army Intelligence Division,

14:20.970 --> 14:23.929
under the pretext of
apprehending a terrorist.

14:23.930 --> 14:25.399
Who are they?

14:25.400 --> 14:27.109
The airport police.

14:27.110 --> 14:30.790
There must have been some kind of
miscommunication between them.

14:43.490 --> 14:45.980
The video ends here.

14:46.470 --> 14:50.399
This shows Skinner being detained
by the Army Intelligence Division.

14:50.400 --> 14:51.790
I think so.

14:52.140 --> 14:53.380
All the reports

14:53.690 --> 14:56.249
about this being a terrorist attack
with biological

14:56.250 --> 14:57.929
or chemical weapons were false?

14:57.930 --> 15:01.659
Since we know Skinner was trying to
smuggle a prototype of Hapna, there's

15:01.660 --> 15:05.920
no doubt that that was the gas-like
substance that leaked from his suitcase.

15:06.430 --> 15:07.770
How could this be?

15:08.140 --> 15:09.700
So you're saying

15:09.840 --> 15:12.499
this prototype reagent

15:12.500 --> 15:13.749
was poten enough to kill instantly?

15:13.750 --> 15:14.830
Yes.

15:15.970 --> 15:19.020
When Skinner returned to the lab
three months later,

15:19.300 --> 15:21.250
he was like a different person.

15:21.750 --> 15:23.359
He shut himself off emotionally

15:23.360 --> 15:25.500
and kept his distance from everyone.

15:25.610 --> 15:27.079
And then six months later,

15:27.080 --> 15:29.989
Hapna appeared in the last place
anyone would expect.

15:29.990 --> 15:30.940
Where?

15:31.140 --> 15:33.470
That was at Ayman Prison in Arizona.

15:34.120 --> 15:37.140
The prison where Axel was incarcerated
at that time.

15:37.810 --> 15:40.510
[Personal Information: Deniz Skinner]

15:38.230 --> 15:40.710
Just as you suspected,

15:40.860 --> 15:44.360
Skinner did undergo an artificial heart
transplant here.

15:44.760 --> 15:46.890
Post-operative reactions were good.

15:47.220 --> 15:49.570
But with artificial hearts,

15:49.840 --> 15:51.969
you never know when or where
something might happen.

15:51.970 --> 15:53.270
What do you mean?

15:53.600 --> 15:55.740
Lately, artificial hearts

15:56.180 --> 16:00.070
all have functions
to monitor heartbeat data.

16:00.360 --> 16:01.139
Then,

16:01.140 --> 16:02.089
through that data,

16:02.090 --> 16:03.890
we can find Skinner's location?

16:04.080 --> 16:05.359
Really?

16:05.360 --> 16:06.299
Of course,

16:06.300 --> 16:09.930
Skinner was going to let us
monitor his heart data.

16:10.140 --> 16:11.409
However,

16:11.410 --> 16:15.349
as soon as he was discharged,
he encrypted his contact information,

16:15.350 --> 16:17.630
making it impossible for us to track him.

16:17.960 --> 16:20.420
We have no way of knowing

16:20.650 --> 16:23.110
where he is or even whether he's
still alive.

16:27.320 --> 16:28.089
What's this?

16:28.090 --> 16:30.999
This is the hard drive
of the information transmission system.

16:31.000 --> 16:32.929
If you analyze the data inside,

16:32.930 --> 16:34.690
you might uncover something.

16:35.000 --> 16:36.510
For example,

16:36.650 --> 16:40.010
who is monitoring
his heartbeat for us, etc.

16:45.810 --> 16:48.319
Millie, thank you so much.

16:48.320 --> 16:49.730
Leland.

16:49.860 --> 16:51.000
As for me,

16:51.560 --> 16:54.160
even though your father died
in that accident,

16:54.470 --> 16:56.149
you're still alive,

16:56.150 --> 16:58.180
and that must mean something.

16:59.400 --> 17:02.089
And your father

17:02.090 --> 17:04.210
used to talk about you a lot.

17:04.819 --> 17:07.140
He once said,

17:07.400 --> 17:10.219
"That child is most like me.

17:10.220 --> 17:13.650
I used to clash with my own parents too.

17:14.250 --> 17:17.650
I think I can understand his feelings,"
and things like that.

17:18.670 --> 17:21.140
Hey. We should get going.

17:21.300 --> 17:23.040
Ah. Okay.

17:23.359 --> 17:24.699
Could I

17:24.700 --> 17:26.530
ask you for one favor?

17:27.250 --> 17:29.279
If you catch Skinner,

17:29.280 --> 17:31.270
please bring him here first.

17:31.830 --> 17:33.309
As his attending physician,

17:33.310 --> 17:34.949
I can't accept him

17:34.950 --> 17:36.290
dying like that.

17:59.670 --> 18:00.899
Well,

18:00.900 --> 18:03.679
thank you for taking the time
to accompany me today.

18:03.680 --> 18:06.320
What are you saying?
It was very rewarding.

18:06.410 --> 18:07.640
And also,

18:08.280 --> 18:10.980
there's something I must tell you.

18:11.410 --> 18:12.830
About you being a spy?

18:13.820 --> 18:15.049
You already knew?

18:15.050 --> 18:17.720
Everyone here has their own reasons.

18:18.380 --> 18:21.930
We all have things
that we can't tell others.

18:26.500 --> 18:29.229
Hey, hey, come on now.

18:29.230 --> 18:30.940
Stop crying.

18:33.140 --> 18:34.740
I'm not crying.

18:35.360 --> 18:36.919
Liar.

18:36.920 --> 18:38.240
Really.

18:42.630 --> 18:43.879
Amazing.

18:43.880 --> 18:45.899
The monitoring process is still running.

18:45.900 --> 18:48.609
Even if we can't directly find Skinner,

18:48.610 --> 18:51.430
we can find the place where he's
being monitored.

18:53.000 --> 18:55.349
Back then, in Eyman Prison,

18:55.350 --> 18:58.649
they conducted an experimental drug trial

18:58.650 --> 19:01.580
on death row and life sentence inmates.

19:01.750 --> 19:04.850
In other words,

19:05.130 --> 19:06.359
Axel was one of the test subjects.

19:06.360 --> 19:08.349
But neither the experimental results

19:08.350 --> 19:10.749
nor the subsequent records
of the prisoners

19:10.750 --> 19:12.419
were left behind.

19:12.420 --> 19:13.679
So, you're saying that Axel

19:13.680 --> 19:16.439
is living proof of the experiment, right?

19:16.440 --> 19:20.169
We still haven't been able to
reach the only doctor

19:20.170 --> 19:22.250
at Eyman Prison who knows about this.

19:22.370 --> 19:23.669
Axel

19:23.670 --> 19:25.470
might know that doctor.

19:32.400 --> 19:33.620
Hersch?

19:33.840 --> 19:35.009
We'll talk later.

19:35.010 --> 19:37.969
I want you to go to
the Witness Protection Center right now.

19:37.970 --> 19:40.899
What did you three men do?

19:40.900 --> 19:42.729
Nothing in particular.

19:42.730 --> 19:44.500
Come on.

19:44.720 --> 19:46.230
Your eyes are all red.

19:46.360 --> 19:47.620
You cried, didn't you?

19:49.400 --> 19:50.640
I didn't.

19:52.210 --> 19:53.410
Hersch called me.

19:53.790 --> 19:55.989
I need to go to
the Witness Protection Center now.

19:55.990 --> 19:57.320
[Analyzing...]

19:56.420 --> 19:57.599
There it is.

19:57.600 --> 19:58.180
Where?

19:58.440 --> 19:59.859
This is...

19:59.860 --> 20:02.439
latitude 73°09' N

20:02.440 --> 20:04.839
and longitude 33°72' E.

20:04.840 --> 20:06.079
Islamabad,

20:06.080 --> 20:07.460
Pakistan.

20:07.910 --> 20:09.850
Pakistan?

20:10.070 --> 20:12.789
When we were checking that
pharmaceutical company back then?

20:12.790 --> 20:15.829
Yes.

20:15.830 --> 20:17.069
The Popcorn Wizard we were
tracking the whole time.

20:17.070 --> 20:19.519
Then I'll contact the local police
immediately.

20:19.520 --> 20:20.930
Hold on.

20:21.290 --> 20:23.689
Popcorn Wizard is moving.

20:23.690 --> 20:25.899
Ordinary tracking won't catch her.

20:25.900 --> 20:28.899
To pinpoint her exact real-time location,

20:28.900 --> 20:31.169
I have to be there on-site myself.

20:31.170 --> 20:32.179
But...

20:32.180 --> 20:34.180
This is probably our last chance!

20:34.500 --> 20:37.080
Please let me go to Pakistan!

20:38.600 --> 20:40.749
You know that's dangerous, right?

20:40.750 --> 20:41.750
Yes.

20:43.190 --> 20:44.229
There's

20:44.230 --> 20:45.350
one condition.

20:47.270 --> 20:49.920
I'll go with you, alright?

20:51.200 --> 20:52.420
Okay!

20:55.190 --> 20:57.859
The drug you were forced to take
while in prison in Arizona

20:57.860 --> 20:59.949
seems to be Hapna's prototype reagent.

20:59.950 --> 21:00.540
What?

21:00.700 --> 21:04.539
Everyone else who took it
most likely died.

21:04.540 --> 21:06.279
Really?

21:06.280 --> 21:08.750
You escaped right after the trial,

21:06.330 --> 21:09.770
[Hersch Lindemann]

21:08.780 --> 21:11.029
so you didn't know.

21:11.030 --> 21:12.999
The only other surviving person involved

21:13.000 --> 21:15.010
is the doctor at Eyman Prison
at that time.

21:13.020 --> 21:18.100
[Hersch Lindemann]

21:15.040 --> 21:16.249
Do you remember him?

21:16.250 --> 21:18.260
Yes, we're close.

21:23.690 --> 21:26.889
I want you to go urgently
and ensure his safety.

21:26.890 --> 21:27.959
Understood.

21:27.960 --> 21:29.679
But

21:29.680 --> 21:31.770
why am I the only one still alive?

21:47.700 --> 21:49.070
Eleina.

21:49.320 --> 21:50.340
What the hell?

21:50.740 --> 21:52.810
Nothing. It's okay.

22:04.840 --> 22:06.150
What?

22:07.000 --> 22:08.840
As fierce as fire in attack;

22:10.650 --> 22:12.680
as steady as a mountain in defense.

22:15.520 --> 22:18.660
[6 Days Left...]

23:50.110 --> 23:54.870
[Next Episode]
[#11 Runnin' with the Devil]
